\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The rank-two area singlet modulo three}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{For the column module #{S=\mathbb F_3^2} of
\ref{fdip-00V7}, every #{2T} matrix has determinant one.
Thus the area covector #{e^1\wedge e^2} is invariant:
the dual action multiplies its top exterior power by
the inverse determinant. Write #{\psi^S_{x,1}} and
#{\psi^S_{x,2}} for the unbarred generators of the
#{S}-fiber at #{x}. The
\vocabk{exterior insertion}{fdip-00WU} of this covector
is the nonzero singlet #{\psi^S_{x,1}\psi^S_{x,2}}.}

\p{This fiber has rank two. The Hurwitz fiber in
\ref{fdip-00WX} has rank #{4} and a different exterior
algebra. The actual decomposition of the latter into
two columns, with its operator compatibility, is the
one in \ref{fdip-00VW}; existence of degree-two
singlets alone identifies neither the fibers nor
their coupled kernels.}
